From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:18:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 043/117] PCI: pwrctrl: add Apple T8010 Wi-Fi sequencing

Add a T8010 WLAN platform-control supplier that selects the UART pins,
initializes the firmware-defined register block on runtime resume and
lets its PMGR domain follow runtime-PM ownership. Include the OF
interface explicitly because the supplier consumes device-tree match
data directly.

The Apple Wi-Fi pwrctrl consumer defers until that supplier is present
and bound, then creates a runtime-PM device link with automatic consumer
cleanup. The link keeps the supplier active while endpoint power is
owned, and the pwrctrl path balances regulator enable, device-wake
deassertion, remove and deferred-probe failures.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 10f5566251eb2692da4bc23539e05f2bba69d7a5
---
